node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-191-Query parameters:
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-192-
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-193-- `offset` — required, exactly once: `-1` or a previously returned offset. Missing, repeated, or malformed values are rejected with `invalid_request` (400).
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-194-- `live` — optional: `long-poll` or `sse`. Any other value is rejected with `invalid_request` (400). Omitted = return immediately with whatever is available.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-195-- `tail` — not supported on this surface; rejected with `invalid_request` (400). A stream suffix can omit message starts, compaction boundaries, and earlier deltas, so it cannot be projected safely.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-196-
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-197-Without `live`, the response is `200`, `Content-Type: application/json`, `Cache-Control: no-store`, with `Stream-Next-Offset` and (when the read reached the head) `Stream-Up-To-Date: true`. The body is a chunk array — empty when nothing was recorded after `offset`.
