node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-301-
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-302-- `position` — a monotonic ordering token: `batch` is the durable batch ordinal the chunk was projected from, `index` its position within that batch's projection. `{ batch, index }` is globally unique and ordered across the conversation; compare lexicographically (`batch`, then `index`) to dedupe redelivered chunks. Otherwise opaque — do not interpret the numbers.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-303-- `conversation-reset` — replace all accumulated state with the embedded [snapshot](#flueconversationsnapshot). Emitted when a batch contains a structural boundary (conversation creation, compaction); the reset subsumes every other chunk of its batch, so a fresh read from `offset=-1` begins with one. The embedded snapshot may already contain settlements — check `snapshot.settlements` as well as `submission-settled` chunks when awaiting an outcome.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-304-- `message-appended` — a complete message (user turn or system signal), in the same message format as the snapshot.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-305-- `message-started` — an assistant response opened. `metadata` carries agent-authored response metadata available at start. Assistant chunks are pre-coalesced: every model step of a submission addresses the submission's first assistant `messageId`, so accumulating parts per `messageId` reproduces the snapshot's one-message-per-response shape. A later `message-started` for an already-open `messageId` is a continuation, not a new message.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-306-- `message-metadata` — agent-authored metadata for an open response; merge onto the message.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md:307:- `data-part` — one named client data write; append a `data-<name>` part.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-308-- `message-delta` — streamed `text` or `reasoning` content; append to the open part of that `kind`, opening one if none is open. A `kind` change or `message-completed` closes the open part.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-309-- `tool-input` / `tool-output` / `tool-output-error` — tool-call lifecycle, correlated by `toolCallId`. Input arrives on the assistant message; outputs update the matching `dynamic-tool` part.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-310-- `message-completed` — the assistant response closed; mark streaming parts `done`.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-311-- `submission-settled` — the terminal outcome of one submission, matching the admission response's `submissionId`.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/reference/streaming-protocol.md-312-- `timestamp` — capture time (ISO 8601) of the underlying durable record, present on boundary chunks (`message-started`, `tool-input`, `tool-output`, `tool-output-error`, `message-completed`, `submission-settled`). `message-delta` deliberately omits it for wire weight; interpolate between stamped boundaries.
