node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-13-A hook is a plain function that you call inside your agent function's body to give your agent one new capability. You can spot hooks by their names — they all start with `use`. Each built-in hook lets your agent hook into a different feature of the Flue runtime:
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-14-
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-15-- [Model](/docs/guide/models/) (`useModel`) selects the LLM that powers the agent.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-16-- [Sandbox](/docs/guide/sandboxes/) (`useSandbox`) provides its filesystem and command-execution environment.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-17-- [Tools](/docs/guide/tools/) (`useTool`) let it call application code and affect external systems.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-18-- [MCP servers](/docs/guide/mcp/) (`useMcpConnection`) mount tools from the open MCP ecosystem.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-19-- [Skills](/docs/guide/skills/) (`useSkill`) provide expertise it can load when needed.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-20-- [Subagents](/docs/guide/subagents/) (`useSubagent`) let it delegate focused work to other agents.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-21-- [Persisted State](#persisted-state) (`usePersistentState`) preserves custom data across the agent lifetime.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-22-- [Event Hooks](#event-hooks) (`useAgentStart`, `useAgentFinish`, and others) trigger logic on different lifecycle events.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md:23:- [Data Writers](#streaming-data-to-the-client) (`useDataWriter`) stream structured data to your client UI.
node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/guide/agent-hooks.md-24-- [Custom Hooks](#custom-hooks) let you compose new hooks out of the built-ins.
