node_modules/@flue/cli/docs/sdk/overview.md:7:The **Flue Agent SDK** (`@flue/sdk`) is the TypeScript client for one agent conversation of a deployed Flue application. A client wraps a single **conversation URL** — the path where the agent's router (`createAgentRouter(...)`) is [mounted](/docs/guide/routing/#mounting-an-agent) plus a caller-chosen conversation id — and exposes typed methods over the HTTP routes that URL serves: admit a message, await its settlement, read or observe the materialized conversation, abort in-flight work, and resolve attachment bytes.
